<section class="problem-hero"><div class="site-shell problem-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Tree and debris roof impact · Charlotte, NC</p><h1>A tree hit the roof. What happens next?</h1><p>Majestic separates immediate safety and temporary protection from the permanent roofing repair, then documents every accessible condition before the roof is closed.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-gold" href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc#claim-form">@Lang.T("Request free inspection →")</a><a class="button button-ghost" href="tel:+19808005991">@Lang.T("Call Majestic")</a></div></div><figure class="problem-hero-visual"><img src="/damage-guides/tree-impact-example.webp" alt="Educational example of tree impact damage on an asphalt shingle roof"/><div class="problem-icon problem-icon-tree" aria-label="TREE"><span></span><i></i><b></b></div><figcaption>@Lang.T("Educational damage example · inspection determines the actual condition")</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="problem-urgent"><div class="site-shell"><strong>@Lang.T("SAFETY FIRST")</strong><p>Stay away from the impact area. If the tree contacts power lines, the structure is shifting, or anyone is in danger, call 911 and the utility first. Do not enter an unstable attic or climb onto the roof.</p></div></section><section class="problem-signs section"><div class="site-shell problem-clues-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("What you may notice")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Visible clues help define the inspection—not the final diagnosis.")</h2><p>@Lang.T("Use these examples to describe what you see from a safe location. A photo cannot confirm every roof layer, hidden moisture, cause or repairability.")</p></div><figure class="problem-clue-photo"><img src="/damage-guides/tree-impact-example.webp" alt="Educational example of tree impact damage on an asphalt shingle roof"/><figcaption>@Lang.T("Educational reference—not a Majestic customer case.")</figcaption></figure><ul><li>Branches or a trunk resting on the roof</li><li>Open shingles, underlayment or decking</li><li>Sagging roof lines or cracked framing</li><li>Damaged gutters, fascia, soffit or vents</li><li>New ceiling stains or active water entry</li></ul></div></section><section class="problem-first section" id="first-steps"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("Before the crew arrives")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Five first steps for the homeowner.")</h2></div><p>@Lang.T("Do only what can be completed safely from the ground or a stable interior area.")</p></div><ol><li><span>01</span><p>Move people and pets away from the affected rooms.</p></li><li><span>02</span><p>Photograph visible conditions from the ground only when safe.</p></li><li><span>03</span><p>Call emergency authorities or the utility for life-safety or electrical hazards.</p></li><li><span>04</span><p>Call Majestic so roof access, weather and temporary protection can be assessed.</p></li><li><span>05</span><p>Preserve receipts, photos and the time the damage was discovered.</p></li></ol></div></section><section class="problem-process section"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading centered-heading"><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("How Majestic handles this specific problem")</p><h2>@Lang.T("A documented path from concern to completed roof.")</h2><p>@Lang.T("The exact scope depends on safe access and what the inspection confirms. These five stages show how this particular roof condition is evaluated and repaired.")</p></div><div class="problem-process-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Safety and access</h3><p>We confirm whether the roof can be approached. Tree removal or structural stabilization may need to happen first.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Temporary protection</h3><p>When conditions are safe, exposed areas may be covered to reduce additional water entry.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Roof and structure inspection</h3><p>We document shingles, underlayment, decking, penetrations, roof edges and visible framing concerns.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Written repair scope</h3><p>The scope separates roofing work from tree service, electrical, structural or interior work that may require another qualified trade.</p></article><article><span>05</span><h3>Repair and closeout</h3><p>Authorized materials are removed and rebuilt in sequence, followed by final photographs, invoice and applicable warranty documents.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="arrival-section section" id="arrival"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("What happens when we arrive")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Six checkpoints from arrival through closeout.")</h2></div><p>@Lang.T("Majestic documents the roof as a construction system, explains choices before work begins and keeps insurance coverage decisions separate from contractor work.")</p></div><div class="arrival-grid"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Arrival, interview and safety check</h3><p>The technician confirms what happened, when the condition was first noticed, whether water is entering now and which interior rooms are affected. Before using a ladder, Majestic checks weather, electrical, tree, structural and fall hazards and explains any access limitation.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Interior and ground-level reference</h3><p>When relevant and accessible, the team starts at the stain, drip or impacted room, reviews the attic from a safe access point and then walks the exterior perimeter. This creates a reference line between the interior evidence and the roof area above it.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Roof-system inspection</h3><p>When safe access is available, Majestic reviews affected slopes plus shingles, ridge and hip caps, valleys, flashing, pipe boots, vents, skylights, roof edges, gutters, fascia and soffit. Wide photographs show location; detail photographs show the condition.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Measurements and factual documentation</h3><p>The record identifies visible conditions, roof geometry, affected components and estimated quantities. Storm-related observations are separated from age, maintenance, installation details and hidden conditions that cannot be confirmed without authorized removal.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h3>Options explained before authorization</h3><p>Majestic explains immediate protection, localized repair, section rebuild and replacement paths when applicable. The homeowner receives a written roofing path and can choose an out-of-pocket project or use the factual documents in a claim they manage with their carrier.</p></div></article><article><span>06</span><div><h3>Construction, verification and closeout</h3><p>After a written scope is approved, materials and schedule are confirmed. Majestic performs the authorized roofing work, controls debris and cleanup, photographs completion and provides the applicable invoice, warranty and project-closeout documents.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="problem-repairs section" id="repairs"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("Repair options")</p><h2>@Lang.T("The inspection determines which option can be built reliably.")</h2></div><p>@Lang.T("Final materials, quantities, code requirements and hidden conditions are confirmed in the written scope.")</p></div><div class="problem-repair-grid"><article><h3>Localized roof repair</h3><p>Remove damaged shingles and underlayment, replace affected decking when verified, restore the water-shedding layers and match materials as closely as practical.</p></article><article><h3>Section rebuild</h3><p>When an impact damages a valley, ridge, eave or multiple components, a larger roof section may need coordinated removal and reconstruction.</p></article><article><h3>Structural coordination</h3><p>Broken rafters, trusses or displaced framing require evaluation and a separate structural repair path before final roofing is completed.</p></article><article><h3>Full replacement</h3><p>Replacement may be considered when damage is widespread, matching is impractical, the system is near the end of service life or a reliable localized repair cannot be built.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="problem-source"><div class="site-shell"><span>i</span><p>Ready.gov advises watching for fallen power lines and trees after thunderstorms. <a href="https://www.ready.gov/thunderstorms-lightning" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the source ↗</a></p></div></section><section class="faq-section section"><div class="site-shell faq-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("FAQ")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Clear expectations before work begins.")</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>@Lang.T("Is the inspection free?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("Yes. Majestic provides a free roof inspection, photographs, a report, estimated measurements and a written project path, subject to safe access.")</p></details><details><summary>@Lang.T("Does the inspection guarantee insurance coverage?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("No. Majestic documents roofing conditions and scope. The carrier independently decides coverage and payment.")</p></details><details><summary>@Lang.T("Can I pay out of pocket?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("Yes. Majestic can explain an out-of-pocket repair or replacement path as well as the construction documentation used for a claim-related project.")</p></details><details><summary>@Lang.T("How far do you travel?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("Roof inspections are available approximately 90 minutes from Charlotte or Rock Hill, subject to address and schedule confirmation. Raleigh is not in the service area.")</p></details></div></div></section><section class="resource-cta section"><div class="site-shell"><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("Free inspection")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Photos, report, estimated measurements and a written project path.")</h2><a class="button button-gold" href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc#claim-form">@Lang.T("Start my request →")</a></div></section>
